{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1503715-wraith-mortals-game","id":1503715,"title":"Wraith: Mortals game.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Wraith: The Oblivion"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-02-22T18:50:15-08:00","id":1503715,"title":"Wraith: Mortals game.","content":"While reading W:tO, I read, &quot;Archaic-Rifle&quot;, and thought, what if I created a Wraith-game, set in the Age of Reason, based on alive-characters in a war between two nations? At the time I found a random city-generator program that could make black and white city maps, and I supposed I could create a map with a Wraith-feel. But when I did a double take at my Wraith-book, there was no character-sheet with mortal health-levels. With the city-generation program, I could make, a &quot;Tale of Two Cities&quot;, that war with each other. I could also add some other suppernatural-element other than the forgone conclusion that the characters will dead and become Wraiths, like witchcraft, but based off of Wraith-powers etc. And I have the <i>Risen</i> book too, so there's that and the game turns into a <i>Crow</i>-sequel.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-23T10:47:06-08:00","id":1503763,"title":"","content":"Mortal characters have 7 Health points.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-23T12:28:10-08:00","id":1503766,"title":"","content":"If you have Wraith20, and don't want to have your PCs start with human sheets, only to switch to wraith sheets later? You can use the Orpheus rules in the back of the book for Corpus-as-Health in still living characters.<br /> <br /> There's actually a lot of cool potential plot hooks even if you never get into the Orpheus group that could highlight the themes of the era in question beyond that. One the precursor drugs to synthetic Pigment could be very popular for one side in the conflict (esp. if their medical supply lines are in trouble), and could be both an established part of the setting for why the PCs all become wraiths (while less true in the older forms, all Pigment users become ghosts even if most stay drones instead of full wraiths) while also prompting some interesting things to explore if the PCs don't want to abandon the base setting to go become part of Stygia instead.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}